      "limits": [
        "Concurrent atomic refcounts are covered; concurrent ownership bitmap mutations are not claimed. The original bitmap mutations were also non-atomic.",
        "Command transport and native completion are doubled."
      ]
    },
    {
      "adapter": "adapt_converted_cache.py",
      "blocking": false,
      "reviewedMechanism": "Absent-range lookup, remove and dependency-add return without creating dictionary/list entries. Existing-entry first-match, cached-null, key equality, disposal and dependency paths remain unchanged.",
      "productionProof": "Whole production CacheByRange, key types and Dependency are compiled by the existing fixture. Final cache composes exactly with the indirect-key delta.",
      "limits": [
        "Inter-range Dictionary enumeration order is unspecified and can differ; tests do not claim preservation.",
        "GPU payload and the invalidation boundary are doubled; no new thread-safety guarantee is claimed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "adapter": "adapt_indirect_cache_key.py",
      "blocking": false,
      "reviewedMechanism": "Making the indirect key and its nested base key mutable prevents SetBuffer from modifying a defensive copy, so disposal invalidates the stored converted index buffer. Structural equality criteria are unchanged.",
      "productionProof": "The complete production indirect conversion caller constructs, sets and boxes the key. The actual cache, dirty-index method, bound-equality method and four cache wrappers are exercised by the existing fixture and match final method hashes.",
      "limits": [
        "Native allocation, shader conversion and graphics binding endpoints are doubled.",
        "This is a cache-coherence correction; no direct performance improvement is asserted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "adapter": "adapt_allocator_blocks.py",
      "blocking": false,
      "reviewedMechanism": "The native allocation remains locally owned until InsertBlock succeeds. Failure cleanup unmaps only after a successful map and frees in a finally block. DedicatedIndex publication, swap removal and replacement-index updates use the existing write lock. Pooled and imported range bookkeeping is preserved.",
      "productionProof": "Existing fixtures compile the complete production allocator, allocation handle and range bookkeeping, including threaded allocate/free workloads. Native calls are strict doubles. Managed setup and publication-boundary failures are injected explicitly.",
      "limits": [
        "Concurrent allocator Dispose versus active allocation/free remains outside the pre-existing contract.",
        "Selection among equal-size pooled blocks may differ. The mixed pool=4096 workload peak rises from 251260 to 255356 bytes; the pool=16 dedicated-only workload preserves exact trace and native peak.",
        "Timers are indicative and not a pass/fail gate. The recorded 32-block churn time rises from 3.649845 to 4.544984 ms, while 2048-block churn falls from 13.493069 to 4.765198 ms. Constant bounded visits, rather than universal elapsed-time improvement, are the deterministic evidence.",
        "The bookkeeping measurement includes all allocations associated with construction: block construction stays at 176 bytes per instance and block-list construction rises by 8 bytes per instance in this host runtime.",
        "The fixture does not use a physical Vulkan driver and injects managed setup/publication faults at explicit boundaries rather than forcing every possible runtime allocation failure."
      ]
    }
